    <description>Quick Action screen flow launched from a customer Contact by the Service Receptionist, for a service walk-in customer who expresses sales interest. recordId is the Contact&apos;s Id; Get_Contact resolves it to that Contact&apos;s Account (Get_Account) since the Opportunity is created under the Account, not the Contact. Captures Brand and preferred dealership (Showroom), creates the Opportunity, and assigns it to the Showroom Manager of that dealership&apos;s Business Unit, with a same-day contact Task (KNOWN SIMPLIFICATION: Task ActivityDate is date-only, so the 15-minute window is approximated as &quot;today&quot;, matching the convention already used by AF_FL_Lead_SLAEscalation). The Showroom Manager&apos;s subsequent reassignment to a Sales Representative — and the notification that follow — is handled centrally by AF_FL_Opp_AfterCreate watching for OwnerId changes on Service Walk-in Opportunities, not duplicated here. Decide_ShowroomManager_Found guards against no active user holding the resolved Showroom Manager role (e.g. a Business Unit with the role not yet staffed) - routes to Screen_NoShowroomManager with a clear message instead of failing the Opportunity create with a blank-owner DML error.</description>
